Source-landscape note: The 2023 U.S. economic-policy source universe is unusually extensive and spans primary legislation, budget and macroeconomic records, implementation audits, central-bank and bank-resolution records, international assessments, academic work, think-tank analyses, investigative journalism, local reporting, and partisan/exculpatory accounts. Key source families include the IIJA, CHIPS Act, IRA, Fiscal Responsibility Act, inflation and labor outcomes, industrial-policy implementation, distribution, antitrust, fiscal sustainability, and the 2023 banking shock. Search saturation was not reached; additional source discovery is warranted.

